  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The East Africa Documentary Film Fund (Docubox) enables talented, driven, and focused East African filmmakers to produce high-impact independent documentary films that unearth new realities about worlds, identities, and people for audiences in East Africa and around the world. Docubox supports filmmakers through production grants, mentorship labs, training, and networking opportunities to create high-quality films that are used to bring about change in society. Docubox aims to deepen these focal areas and launch the next phase of the Get Reel project to produce impactful films addressing sexual and reproductive health, rights, and justice, as well as conduct community impact screenings across East Africa. (Strategy: Global Reproductive Equity)</narrative>
  </description>
